    turnFlow: 'First player leads any tile and declares which end is open. Each turn, in counter-clockwise order: play a tile matching the open end (the other end becomes the new open end; if a double is played the open end stays the same) or discard one tile face down. Discarded tiles are kept in front of the player until the end. When all tiles are played or discarded, players expose discards and count pips. Fewest pips wins; that player leads the next deal. Tie for fewest: whoever played earlier in the deal (previous first player has priority, then to the right).',
