    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 8 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Play tiles matching the single open end of the layout or discard when unable; the player with fewest total pips on discarded tiles wins the deal. Pairs settle by pip difference (stake per pip agreed in advance).',
      'Turn-flow example: First player leads any tile and declares which end is open. Each turn, in counter-clockwise order: play a tile matching the open end (the other end becomes the new open end; if a double is played the open end stays the same) or discard one tile face down. Discarded tiles are kept in front of the player until the end. When all tiles are played or discarded, players expose discards and count pips. Fewest pips wins; that player leads the next deal. Tie for fewest: whoever played earlier in the deal (previous first player has priority, then to the right).',
      'Scoring example: After all tiles are played or discarded, each player exposes discarded tiles and counts total pips. The player with fewest pips wins the deal. Each pair of players settles by pip difference; stake per pip is agreed in advance; the player with more pips pays the player with fewer. The player with fewest total pips on discarded tiles wins the deal and leads the next. Tie: whoever played earlier in the deal (previous first player has priority, then to the right)..',
